# What must never reach the image.
#
# `COPY . .` takes the working tree as it stands, so anything sitting beside the
# source ships inside the image and stays in its layers. Without this file the
# image contained the live .env — Cloudflare token, database password and
# SECRET_KEY — the development database, and the unredacted scan reports. None
# of that is recoverable by deleting the files in a later layer: the earlier
# layer still holds them, and anyone who pulls the image can read it.
#
# It is also why builds were flaky and slow. The context was 206 MB, 193 MB of
# it a Windows virtualenv, checksummed over a 9p mount on every build.

# Secrets. The container gets its configuration from the environment at run
# time; the file itself has no business being inside.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
config/caddy/certs/
config/caddy/dns/

# A host virtualenv is the wrong platform and the wrong Python.
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local state. The container mounts volumes for these.
data/
staticfiles/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*

# The originals behind the scan-report corpus: real VINs, real vehicles. The
# redacted .words.json captures beside them are safe and stay, so a test run
# inside the container still has a corpus to work with.
Artifacts/samples/**/*.pdf
Artifacts/samples/*.jpg
Artifacts/samples/**/*.jpeg
Artifacts/samples/**/*.png
Artifacts/samples/backups/
Data/

# History, tooling and editor noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.md
!README.md
docs/
locale/*/LC_MESSAGES/*.po

# Compose builds the image; the image does not need to describe itself.
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
